{
  "manifest": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "body": "# ML Task 5 Diagnostic: Profitability vs Selection Edge",
        "id": "title",
        "type": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "body": "## Technical summary\n\n- Profitability was present: **13/13** real arms had positive mean net R at doubled friction.\n- M3 added **+0.0900R** versus same-date random, but constant/equal added **+0.1169R**; M3 trailed it by **-0.0269R**.\n- **8/260** aggregated permutations cleared the real-arm economic gate. Result: profitable opportunity set, no validated unique ranking edge; Task 5 remains STOP.",
        "id": "summary",
        "sourceId": "task5_diagnostic",
        "type": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "body": "## Key findings\n\n- M3 was profitable in **6/8** validation years and beat constant/equal in only **4/8**.\n- M3 and constant/equal shared **0.2%** of selections per date; zero overlap occurred on **1,924/1,936** dates.\n- M3 top-10 symbol share was **30.5%** versus **100.0%** for constant/equal; this exposes the tie-break artifact.\n- Constant/equal is the alphabetical tie-break under equal scores. Its top three symbols supplied **98.9%** of rows; its performance is a roster/cohort artifact, not an equal-weight baseline.",
        "id": "findings",
        "sourceId": "task5_diagnostic",
        "type": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "chartId": "baseline_comparison",
        "id": "baseline_chart",
        "type": "chart"
      },
      {
        "chartId": "year_comparison",
        "id": "year_chart",
        "type": "chart"
      },
      {
        "id": "fold_table",
        "tableId": "fold_comparison",
        "type": "table"
      },
      {
        "id": "regime_table",
        "tableId": "regime_comparison",
        "type": "table"
      },
      {
        "id": "symbol_table",
        "tableId": "symbol_concentration",
        "type": "table"
      },
      {
        "body": "## Scope, data, and methodology\n\nExact A-T1-M3 and constant/equal top-3 selections were reconstructed for the four locked walk-forward folds from the hash-verified 2011\u20132023 Track A shards. Each fold retained the locked 15-session purge/embargo, doubled friction, and 100-replicate same-date random control. Model, baseline, and control hashes match Task 5. No 2024+ row was read.",
        "id": "methodology",
        "sourceId": "task5_diagnostic",
        "type": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "id": "permutation",
        "tableId": "permutation_table",
        "type": "table"
      },
      {
        "body": "## Limitations and robustness\n\n- The 15-session outcomes are overlapping event labels, not a slot- or capital-constrained 2\u20133-week portfolio backtest.\n- The roster is survivor-only; adjusted history may include later source revisions. Absolute profit is development evidence only.\n- With 260 controls, an independent 1% false-positive rate implies **92.7%** chance of at least one clear. The controls are dependent, so this is diagnostic context, not a retroactive threshold change.\n- A-T1-M3 had **0/20** local permutation clears; all eight family-level clears were Track B arms.\n- This post-hoc report cannot create candidates, amend STOP, or authorize Task 6.",
        "id": "limitations",
        "sourceId": "task5_diagnostic",
        "type": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "body": "## Next steps\n\nNone authorized. Preserve Task 5 STOP. Any redesigned multiplicity rule, point-in-time universe, or slot-constrained portfolio test requires a new preregistered task.",
        "id": "next_steps",
        "type": "markdown"
      }
    ],
